(7671662, 1252142, 67145, '<td valign="top">meant to comment before when I saw it in voting and again yesterday  .. <br/>I''ll blame my really slow internet .. <br/>took two minutes for a photo to load yesterday .. and that''s my story  ..!! .. <br/>non fiction btw .. <br/>anyway .. this is truly and stunning and powerful image .. it really brings home the power of nature .. <br/>but also there''s this clinging to life feel .. almost like a sadness and loneliness .. <br/>that little tree .. all alone in a tempest .. so close to the brink .. <br/>I''m sure many ppl have felt the same .. <br/></td>', 'meant to comment before when I saw it in voting and again yesterday  .. I''ll blame my really slow internet .. took two minutes for a photo to load yesterday .. and that''s my story  ..!! .. non fiction btw .. anyway .. this is truly and stunning and powerful image .. it really brings home the power of nature .. but also there''s this clinging to life feel .. almost like a sadness and loneliness .. that little tree .. all alone in a tempest .. so close to the brink .. I''m sure many ppl have felt the same .. ', '2020-08-05 22:04:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(7671663, 1252119, 181847, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Farmr:</b></div><hr/><i> Very Nice,  Sun on one side, stars on the other.... </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Not the Sun but rather nearly Full Moon that had just rose above the horizon. <br/> <br/>This was shot June 6, 2020. -- This is a very popular location for sunrise shots where the bottom of the arch is aglow with sunlight. I had often thought that a moon rise might have the same effect. The June full moon is known as the Rose Moon. Wind in the area had a lot of the red desert dust in the air. When the moon rose it was almost red. I waited until the night after the full moon so that moon rise was well after sunset at the end of the Blue Hour.</td>', 'Originally posted by Farmr: Very Nice,  Sun on one side, stars on the other....   Not the Sun but rather nearly Full Moon that had just rose above the horizon.  This was shot June 6, 2020. -- This is a very popular location for sunrise shots where the bottom of the arch is aglow with sunlight. I had often thought that a moon rise might have the same effect. The June full moon is known as the Rose Moon. Wind in the area had a lot of the red desert dust in the air. When the moon rose it was almost red. I waited until the night after the full moon so that moon rise was well after sunset at the end of the Blue Hour.', '2020-08-05 22:07:50.000000', NULL, 0),
